From 2c0329e8586d762c9cdfa0a3b4d1ce2c24dd8220 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 08:53:02 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 23/25] Video and canvas: an element's opacity on its image

An opacity on a <video> or <canvas> made an off-screen surface of the
element, drawn once and composited with the opacity. Both are one image,
so they now take the opacity themselves (CanApplyOpacity), as other
image items do: the async image pipeline carries it
(OpUpdateAsyncImagePipeline::opacity) to the image it draws (the image's
color, DisplayListBuilder::SetImageOpacity), and YUV images gain an
opacity in WebRender (YuvImageDisplayItem::opacity, brush_yuv_image).
The image stays in the page's tiles, where a stereo picture is drawn
once per eye. A video's opacity reaches its image past the empty
overlays of its controls and captions: a blend container that paints
nothing takes no opacity (CollectItemsWithOpacity). An image drawn with
an opacity is never promoted to a compositor surface, which would show
it opaque.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5 via Claude Code
